        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-6">Why landscaping is not like other trades</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-5">A plumber can drive across the county for one emergency call and still make money on it. A landscaping crew cannot. Your margin lives in route density — fifteen properties on three streets beats fifteen properties spread across forty miles, every single week, forever.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed mb-5">That changes what good marketing looks like. An agency that measures success in raw lead count will happily send you estimates from forty minutes away and call it a win. We measure whether the leads cluster where your trucks already are.</p>
        <p class="text-gray-500 leading-relaxed">The second difference is revenue shape. Mowing contracts are your floor — predictable, unglamorous, and what keeps the crew paid in a slow month. Design, install, hardscape and irrigation are where the margin is. A marketing plan that only feeds one of those is only doing half the job.</p>
      </div>
